{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:1c7e440aa825d547","name":"Imperial Knight (CL 10)","source":{"id":"source:reference-1c7e440aa825d547","title":"Imperial Knight (CL 10)","revision":25227,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:11:29Z","sha256":"f2975e9f7f3b342371e4f421691e6e8781797133cedd90f4a99d49dced80d029","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25227","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Imperial%20Knight%20%28CL%2010%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-1c7e440aa825d547","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Fel Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Fel_Empire","referenceId":"reference:45bef1c82bffe9c1"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}," are members of a Force-using tradition that arises during the time of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Krayt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Krayt","referenceId":"reference:c6d0b6bc88280f92"},", some 130 years following the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},". Like Jedi Knights, the Imperial Knights were trained in the ways of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," including the use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},". Unlike ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", however, Imperial Knights swore fealty to the Emperor of the period, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Roan_Fel","referenceId":"reference:b68838dc4018d9d2"},", above all else. As such, members of the New Jedi Order did not recognize the Imperial Knights as true Jedi.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Of the traits that set Imperial Knights apart from their Jedi cousins, the most prominent were their use of silver-bladed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," and red ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battle Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battle_Armor","referenceId":"reference:ba57c05b399c4316"},". Perhaps the most interesting affectation used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}," were gauntlets composed of cortosis weave, which would cause any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," blade that came into contact with them to become nonfunctional.  When a Sith Lord proclaimed himself Emperor, the Imperial Knights who survived the coup worked with the former Emperor in an effort to bring down the usurper. Though only a small number of Imperial Knights are thought to have survived the coup, it is possible that others managed to do so.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Imperial Knight Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["During the time of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Krayt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Krayt","referenceId":"reference:c6d0b6bc88280f92"},", Imperial Knights acted as the sworn protectors of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emperor Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emperor_Roan_Fel"},". As such, they are rarely encountered away from the Emperor. Following the coup by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Krayt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Krayt","referenceId":"reference:c6d0b6bc88280f92"}," that put the Sith Lord on the galactic throne, the Imperial Knights who remained behind might be found anywhere, working to put a stop to the new Emperor's rule.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Tactically, Imperial Knights are similar to Jedi. They work well together, using their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," to redirect blaster shots against their foes until they can close to melee range. When fighting other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"-wielding Force-users, Imperial Knights attempt to use their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cortosis Gauntlets"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cortosis_Gauntlets"}," to deactivate their enemies' weapons for a few minutes. Given their loyalty to their Emperor, Imperial Knights are less concerned with maintaining a balance between light and dark. As such, some might employ powers that are normally designated as Dark Side.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Imperial Knight Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," 7/",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Knight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Knight","referenceId":"reference:8a1e23d924066b37"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 6; ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"t